    "id": "heattrak-walkway-mat-20x60",
    "name": "HeatTrak Heated Walkway Mat with Power Unit (20 x 60 in)",
    "category": "20 x 60 in Walkway Mat, Power Unit Included, 2 in/hr, Down to -8°F (Listed)",
    "badge": "Best Overall",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Power unit included, so it plugs in and runs out of the box",
      "Listed melt rate of 2 inches of snow per hour",
      "Surface runs about 40°F above the air temperature, per HeatTrak",
      "Other HeatTrak stair and walkway mats daisy-chain from it",
      "2-year manufacturer's warranty from the date of shipment"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "The listing does not give this mat's own amp draw",
      "Power unit limit is listed as 13 amps here but 14 amps on other HeatTrak listings",
      "Not sold or rated for driving over"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The best heated walkway mat for most homes: a 5-foot mat with its own power unit that can grow into a full HeatTrak system.",
    "description": "If you want one snow melting mat that works the day it arrives and can grow into a whole system later, start here. This is HeatTrak's 20 by 60 inch walkway mat sold with the power unit, which the listing describes as the first mat in a HeatTrak setup: it plugs into the outlet and every other HeatTrak stair or walkway mat daisy-chains from it. HeatTrak lists a melt rate of 2 inches of snow per hour, a surface that runs about 40 degrees Fahrenheit above the air temperature, and good performance down to -8 degrees Fahrenheit. That last figure matters more than the melt rate: below it, the mat is warmer than the air but may not stay above freezing, so very cold regions should expect slower clearing. The power unit is listed as handling a configuration of mats up to 13 amps, though other HeatTrak listings say 14 amps, so confirm the figure on the unit itself before you plan a long chain. The listing does not state this mat's own amp draw, so check the label or HeatTrak's spec sheet when you add mats. It carries a 2-year warranty. The trade-off is cost per foot: a full path of these adds up quickly. If you only need one doorstep cleared, the Cozy Products Ice-Away is simpler; if you need steps too, the Starter Kit is better value."
  },
  {
    "id": "heattrak-starter-kit",
    "name": "HeatTrak Snow Melting Mats Starter Kit (1 Walkway Mat, 2 Stair Mats)",
    "category": "20 x 60 in Walkway + Two 10 x 30 in Stair Mats, Power Unit, Cable Extender",
    "badge": "Best for Steps and Walk",
